course: dictionary
lesson: 3421
title: Extension
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An extension is an extra part added to something to make it bigger or longer. Read the words around it to find its meaning. «If a lesson is too easy, you can politely ask the teacher for a harder challenge, because teachers often have extension work.» Here, extension work means extra, harder tasks for pupils who finish early.
explain: The same word can mean different things in different places. «...whether people may build big extensions» means extra rooms or parts added onto a house. An extension lead is a cable that makes a plug reach further. Hair extensions are extra hair added to make hair look longer.
explain: Extension can also mean extra time to finish a job. If your teacher gives you an extension, your homework is due later than planned. Ask yourself what the sentence is about: a building, a cable, a task, or time. That tells you which meaning fits.
fact: An extension is an extra part added to make something bigger or longer.
fact: An extension can also mean extra time given to finish something.
fact: «Extension work» means harder tasks for pupils who finish early.
fact: An extension lead is a cable that makes a plug reach further, but do not overload it.
fact: An extension telephone number is an extra number inside an office.
exercise: The teacher says, «Here is some extension work for you.» What does extension work mean? | * Harder tasks for pupils who finish early | Work done only at the weekend | Work you do with a pen | Work that is shorter than usual
exercise: Dad says, «Do not overload the extension lead.» What is an extension lead? | A list of phone numbers | A ladder for climbing onto the roof | * A cable that makes a plug reach further
exercise: «They want to build an extension onto the back of their house.» Find and copy one word that means an extra part added to a building. | build | * extension | house | they
test: «They want to build an extension onto the back of their house.» What is an extension here? | A new hole in the garden wall | A small car parked outside | A sheet of paper with notes on it | * A new part added to make the house bigger
test: Sam says, «I asked for an extension to finish my project.» What did Sam ask for? | * More time to finish his project | A bigger project with more pages | A longer cable for his computer | A shorter day at school
exam: Which meaning of extension fits «She asked for an extension to finish her essay»? | A longer cable for the lamp | An extra telephone number at work | * Extra time to finish | A new room built onto her home
